# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Stripe, Google and app-store checklists all ask for a "privacy policy URL" and a
# "terms of service URL". People (and those checklists) guess /privacy-policy and
# /terms-of-service; our real pages are /privacy and /terms. Rather than let those
# guesses 404 — which reads as "this business has no policy" — send them to the
# page that exists. 301 so the correction sticks in caches and search engines.
/privacy-policy /privacy 301
/privacy-policy/* /privacy 301
/privacy_policy /privacy 301
/terms-of-service /terms 301
/terms-of-service/* /terms 301
/tos /terms 301

# The app lives on console.packory.app. People (and old notes/bookmarks) type
# packory.app/admin or packory.app/dashboard and land on this static site, where
# those routes do not exist — the 404 reads as "the admin page is broken", and
# logging in cannot fix it because there is nothing to log into here. Send every
# app path to the console: its middleware then handles auth properly
# (anonymous → /login?next=…, signed-in owner → the page).
/admin https://console.packory.app/admin 301
/admin/* https://console.packory.app/admin/:splat 301
/dashboard https://console.packory.app/dashboard 301
/dashboard/* https://console.packory.app/dashboard/:splat 301
/login https://console.packory.app/login 301
/signup https://console.packory.app/signup 301
